{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02777",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.86,
      "end_seconds": 4.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Okay, so hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.8,
      "end_seconds": 10.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.09,
      "end_seconds": 21.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "I, I wanted to get fainting on exertion looked at. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.64,
      "end_seconds": 27.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.38,
      "end_seconds": 39.91,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "Let me think, it's been going on for one week. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.14,
      "end_seconds": 50.58,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.58,
      "end_seconds": 61.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.82,
      "text": "Honestly, once or twice a day. I notice it more with exertion. I've also had swollen ankles, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.89,
      "end_seconds": 76.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "A few quick ones: cough, leg pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.72,
      "end_seconds": 83.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.51,
      "end_seconds": 86.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.85,
      "end_seconds": 91.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "No, you know, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.39,
      "end_seconds": 96.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.73,
      "end_seconds": 99.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.92,
      "end_seconds": 117.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.04,
      "end_seconds": 121.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.2,
      "end_seconds": 126.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.91,
      "end_seconds": 140.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.64,
      "text": "Okay, so it's sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day. It's furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning for the fluid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.31,
      "end_seconds": 144.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.3,
      "end_seconds": 148.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "About a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.44,
      "end_seconds": 154.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.38,
      "end_seconds": 165.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days. My partner and our baby. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.81,
      "end_seconds": 180.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.68,
      "end_seconds": 185.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I had part of my thyroid removed years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.64,
      "end_seconds": 192.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.27,
      "end_seconds": 200.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for two years now. Mm, I've had heart failure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.35,
      "end_seconds": 206.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.33,
      "end_seconds": 219.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.87,
      "end_seconds": 248.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 90 percent, pulse is 101 beats a minute. And temperature is 37.2 degrees, BP is 129 over 87."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.12,
      "end_seconds": 255.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.54,
      "end_seconds": 257.24,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.46,
      "end_seconds": 261.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "So, I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.25,
      "end_seconds": 278.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "There is a loud second heart sound and a raised jugular pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.65,
      "end_seconds": 298.1,
      "duration_seconds": 17.45,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Okay, so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is possible pulmonary hypertension. I'll request an ECG, it'll help with syncope. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.03,
      "end_seconds": 301.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.71,
      "end_seconds": 307.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an echocardiogram because of exertional syncope."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.32,
      "end_seconds": 311.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Mm, how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.18,
      "end_seconds": 327.5,
      "duration_seconds": 15.32,
      "text": "No exertion for now, I am arranging urgent specialist tests. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. I'd like to see you again in one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.93,
      "end_seconds": 329.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.09,
      "end_seconds": 335.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.02,
      "end_seconds": 345.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Let me think, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.1,
      "end_seconds": 350.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}